# CSS document flow (always on)

**Golden sentence:** Layout is a **containing-block** problem. Pick the right display mode for each box. Never invent a second layout system to paper over the first.

ADR: `docs/adr/0007-natural-document-flow.md`. Twin (Studio panes): `layout.mdc`.

## Audience — who follows what

| Surface | Path | Follow |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **General CSS / Tailwind** | Studio chrome **and** ideal-stack (`projects/*`) | **§ General practice** — MDN / Flexbox / Chrome-aligned |
| **Studio chrome policy** | `apps/studio/**` only | **§ Studio policy** — stricter product recipes (rails, DeskPane, chat) |

Ideal-stack does **not** inherit Studio’s “overflow-only / no `min-w-0`” default — that is Studio chrome taste. Ideal-stack still follows general facts, sparse flex/grid, and “no escape-hatch creativity.”

Tone in both sections: **Must / Must not / Recipe**. No inventing a 4th layout system.

---

## CSS facts (why — MDN / CSSWG)

| # | Fact | Fail if ignored |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **Normal flow** — block boxes stack; inlines run; block width = containing block | `flex-col` “to stack” |
| 2 | **Containing block** — usually content box of nearest block/flex/grid ancestor | Child “won’t shrink” — parent never got a definite width |
| 3 | **Flex/grid** create a formatting context — children leave normal flow | Nested flex/grid = second min-size graph |
| 4 | Flex item default **`min-width`/`min-height: auto`** = content minimum | Long title / `<button>` blows past the pane |
| 5 | Overflow ≠ `visible` → that auto minimum becomes **0** (item can shrink) — **same effect as `min-width: 0`** | Wrong overflow placement; or clipping menus that must paint outside |
| 6 | **`overflow-y: auto`** + definite height = **scrollport** | `overflow-hidden` on the thing that should scroll |
| 7 | **`<button>` has intrinsic sizing** — not a normal block | Expecting bare `block`+`truncate` without flex-item + overflow/min-size |
| 8 | **Sticky** sticks to nearest scroll ancestor; margins affect stick math | Surprise gaps / early unstick |
| 9 | **Grid** = 2D track skeleton; **flex** = 1D peer row/column | Content `grid-cols-1` “for truncation” |
| 10 | **Percentage** width/height need a definite containing size | Cargo-cult `w-full` / `h-full` instead of tracks |
| 11 | **`contain` / `container-type`** = isolation + **container queries** — not a truncate recipe | Using `contain-inline-size` to fake narrow-rail width |

**Sources:** [MDN flow layout](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Display/Flow_layout) · [Flexbox §4.5 automatic minimum size](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-flexbox-1/#min-size-auto) · [Chrome modern-web-guidance — CSS layout](https://github.com/GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance/blob/main/skills/modern-web-guidance/guides/css-layout/css-layout.md) · [Jake Archibald — page layout](https://jakearchibald.com/2014/dont-use-flexbox-for-page-layout/)

