## § General practice (Studio + ideal-stack)

Applies everywhere Tailwind/`@theme` UI ships. Matches industry CSS guidance.

### Three boxes

| Box | Job | Tailwind skeleton |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **A. Shell / page band** | Split viewport or major regions into tracks | **One** `grid` *or* outer `flex` |
| **B. Pane column** | Fill leftover height; pin chrome; one scroll leaf | `flex flex-col overflow-hidden` → child `flex-1 overflow-y-auto` |
| **C. Content** | Document / list / form / marketing band | **Block/inline** default; **one** `flex`/`inline-flex` for peer rows; **grid OK** when the node is a true **2D track skeleton** |

**Must not** invent a 4th box: content `grid-cols-1` / nested `grid-rows` / `contain-*` **as layout escape hatches** for truncation.

### Decision tree

```
1. Viewport / major region track split (or true 2D component skeleton)?
   → YES: grid (or outer flex) ONCE for that job. Stop.
2. Pane (chrome + filling body + chrome)?
   → YES: pane recipe (Law G3). Stop.
3. Siblings in one row (icon+label, avatar+bubble)?
   → YES: ONE flex/inline-flex parent. Truncate/shrink on sharing children. Stop.
4. Else:
   → Block/inline. space-y / margins. truncate on text if needed.
   → Truncate fails? Fix ancestry — do NOT invent grid-cols-1 / contain-* hacks.
```

### Laws G1–G10 (general)

#### Law G1 — Default is normal flow

| Must | Must not |
| --- | --- |
| New wrappers: **no** `flex` / `grid` unless this node arranges **peers**, a **pane**, a **shell/page band**, or a **2D track skeleton** | `flex flex-col` for stacking or gap alone → use `space-y-*` / margins |

#### Law G2 — One layout parent per concern

| Must | Must not |
| --- | --- |
| At most **one** flex/grid ancestor per layout job | Flex/grid on section + group + row + title |

#### Law G3 — Pane recipe (app columns / rails)

```
[pane]    flex flex-col overflow-hidden
  [chrome]  shrink-0
  [scroll]  flex-1 overflow-x-hidden overflow-y-auto   ← ONLY scrollport
  [chrome]  shrink-0
```

| Must not |
| --- |
| Nested scrollports for the same list |
| `grid` / `grid-rows` for the scroll leaf “to fill” |

#### Law G4 — Overflow placement is surgical

| Need | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Pane can shrink in a flex parent | `overflow-hidden` on the **pane** |
| List / log scrolls | `overflow-y-auto` on the **scroll leaf only** |
| Flex child must not widen the track | `overflow-hidden` / `overflow-x-auto` **or** `min-w-0` / `min-inline-size: 0` on **that flex child** |
| Text ellipsis | That child (or its text) also `truncate` |

| Must not |
| --- |
| `overflow-hidden` on every ancestor “to be safe” (clips popovers/tooltips) |
| `contain-inline-size` / `contain-*` as a **layout/truncate** system |

**OK:** `container-type: inline-size` (and Tailwind `@container`) for **container queries** — that is not a truncate hack.

#### Law G5 — Truncation recipe (narrow columns / list buttons)

```
[scroll] flex flex-col flex-1 overflow-x-hidden overflow-y-auto
  [row]    flex … overflow-hidden   (or min-w-0)   ← flex ITEM of scroll
    [title] overflow-hidden truncate
```

Optional: section wrapper `contents` so rows stay flex items of the scroll leaf.

| Must not |
| --- |
| Content `grid` / `grid-cols-1` “to force width” |
| `contain-inline-size` for truncate |
| Layout `max-w-*` clamps on leaves to fake the track |

#### Law G6 — Grid = 2D track skeletons

| Must | Must not |
| --- | --- |
| Grid when the node needs **rows AND columns** (page shell, card internals with tracks, form “label \| field”, marketing section tracks, Design atlas) | Content `grid` / `grid-cols-1` to force truncate or fill a 1D list |
| Prefer **one** grid per concern; subgrid when grandchildren must align to parent tracks | Nested content grids fighting a parent shell grid for **fill/scroll** |

Detail for Studio panes: `layout.mdc`.

#### Law G7 — Fill with tracks; percentages sparingly

| Must | Must not |
| --- | --- |
| Grow with `flex-1` / `1fr` under a real flex/grid parent | Cargo-cult `w-full` / `h-full` on every wrapper |
| **OK:** `w-full` / `inline-size: 100%` on **replaced media** (`img`, video, iframe) with `aspect-ratio` inside a definite containing block | `w-full` / `h-full` as the **pane fill** instead of `flex-1` |

#### Law G8 — Sticky chrome

| Must | Must not |
| --- | --- |
| `sticky` + inset (`top-0`) + opaque bg when covering content | Assume sticky works across an `overflow` ancestor that isn’t the intended scrollport |

**Scrollport section headers (lists):** prefer **no margin** on the sticky node — margins create gap bands when stuck. Marketing sticky nav may use margin; verify against the real scrollport.

#### Law G9 — Semantic HTML first

| Must | Must not |
| --- | --- |
| Real landmarks/controls (`nav`, `button`, …) | `div` soup + grid/flex to fake structure |

#### Law G10 — No escape-hatch creativity

If layout fights → **wrong box or wrong overflow/min-size placement**.

| Must not add |
| --- |
| `contain-*` for **layout/truncate** (CQ `container-type` stays OK) |
| Content `grid-cols-1` / nested `grid-rows` for fill/truncate |
| `!important` layout wars |
| Measure → `style` / `getBoundingClientRect` for everyday layout |

### Tailwind cheat sheet (general)

| Intent | Tailwind | Never |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Stack blocks | *(none)* / `space-y-*` | `flex flex-col` for gap alone |
| Peer row | `flex` / `inline-flex` + `gap-*` | flex on the text leaf |
| Pane column | `flex flex-col overflow-hidden` | nested `grid-rows` for scroll |
| Scroll leaf | `flex-1 overflow-x-hidden overflow-y-auto` | `overflow-hidden` alone on leaf |
| Grow in track | `flex-1` / `1fr` | `h-full` as pane fill |
| Don’t widen track | overflow on flex child **or** `min-w-0` | spray both everywhere |
| Ellipsis | `truncate` on the shrinking text | clip via distant parent only |
| 2D skeleton | one `grid` … | `grid-cols-1` to fake width |
| Media fill | `w-full` + `aspect-ratio` OK | percentage height wars |
| CQ | `@container` / `container-type` | `contain-inline-size` as truncate |

