## § Studio chrome policy (`apps/studio/**` only)

Stricter product law for DeskPane, rails, chat, settings. **Ideal-stack agents: skip this section** unless building Studio-like app chrome.

### Why stricter

Agents over-applied `min-w-0`, content `grid`, and `contain-inline-size` in Studio rails. Studio defaults to the **overflow-on-flex-child** recipe (spec-equivalent to `min-width: 0` per Flexbox §4.5) so the decision tree stays one path.

### Policy S1 — Prefer overflow; `min-w-0` is last resort

| Default (Studio) | Exception |
| --- | --- |
| Flex child that must shrink → `overflow-hidden` / `overflow-x-auto` (not `min-w-0`) | Child must shrink **and** must **not** clip (menus, popovers, absolute children that paint outside) → **`min-w-0` / `min-inline-size: 0` OK** |

| Must not (Studio) |
| --- |
| New `min-w-0` / `min-h-0` as the first reflex on every flex item |
| `overflow-hidden` high in the tree that clips intentional overlays |

### Policy S2 — Grid in product chrome is shell-first

| Must (Studio chrome) | Must not |
| --- | --- |
| Body / stage tracks = grid once; panes = Law G3 flex | Content `grid` inside chat, recents rails, settings lists, empty states |
| Design atlas / true 2D chrome tools may use component grid | `grid-cols-1` “to make truncate work” |

### Policy S3 — No percentage fill for panes

| Must | Must not |
| --- | --- |
| Pane fill = `flex-1` / shell `1fr` | New `w-full` / `h-full` on chrome wrappers for fill |
| Media / iframe preview surfaces may use `w-full` + aspect when the containing track is definite | Percentage height chains through DeskPane |

### Policy S4 — Sticky list headers: no margin

Recents / day headers / sticky section labels in scrollports: **`sticky top-0` + opaque `bg-*`, no `mb-*` / list `py-*` gap bands**.

### Policy S5 — DeskPane / dual-face stay in shell rules

Overflow bands + scroll leaf: `shell/studio-windows.mdc`. No `!important` / DP wars: `shell/chrome-css.mdc`.

### Studio truncation recipe (locked)

```
[scroll] flex flex-col flex-1 overflow-x-hidden overflow-y-auto
  [row]    flex … overflow-hidden          ← flex ITEM (not min-w-0 by default)
    [title] overflow-hidden truncate
```

### Studio checklist (extra)

- [ ] General laws G1–G10 held
- [ ] No new `min-w-0` unless popover/clip exception (S1)
- [ ] No content `grid` in rails/chat/settings lists (S2)
- [ ] No `w-full`/`h-full` pane fill (S3)
- [ ] Sticky section headers: no margin (S4)
- [ ] Truncate = overflow flex item + `truncate` — not grid/contain

